title: room.enter
---
<<if $hasLens>>
<<hide mantelLens>>
<<endif>>
<<if not $metToby>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
<<hide toby>>
The fire is lit. Fog presses at the windows of 221B. #line:100-001
Watson: Nothing in the papers tonight, Holmes. London has gone quiet. #line:100-002
Hero: London is never quiet, Watson. It is only waiting. #line:100-003
<<sound 132>>
<<animate door once>>
<<show mrsHudson>>
<<walk mrsHudson 276 172>>
Mrs Hudson: A young man to see you, Mr Holmes. He's in a dreadful state. #line:100-004
<<show toby>>
<<walk toby 241 180>>
<<walk mrsHudson 285 148>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
<<cel door 0>>
Toby: Mr Holmes? Toby Vance, sir. It's the guv'nor. He's gone. #line:100-005
<<set $metToby to true>>
<<else>>
<<hide mrsHudson>>
<<if $tookCase>>
<<hide toby>>
<<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: room.look
---
The sitting room at 221B. Books, papers and chemicals, in an order only Holmes understands. #line:100-006
===

title: toby.talk
---
-> Your master?
    Toby: Mr Elias Thorne, sir. Clockmaker, Clerkenwell. Three years I've been his apprentice. #line:100-007
    Toby: He was at his bench when I went home last night. This morning the shop's shut up tight, and him gone. #line:100-008
    <<set $askedMaster to true>>
-> The door was locked?
    Toby: Bolted, sir. From the inside. Had to fetch a constable to break it in. #line:100-009
    Hero: And the window? #line:100-010
    Toby: Latched. Nobody got out that way, sir. Couldn't have. #line:100-011
    <<set $askedDoor to true>>
-> The clocks?
    Toby: That's what turned me cold, sir. Every clock on them walls, stopped. All at the same minute. Seventeen past three. #line:100-012
    Toby: All bar the big case clock in the corner. That one was still going. #line:100-013
    <<set $askedClocks to true>>
-> The lantern?
    Toby: Still burning when we broke in. He never leaves it lit, sir. Never. #line:100-014
    <<set $askedLantern to true>>
-> We shall go at once. <<if $askedMaster and $askedDoor and $askedClocks and $askedLantern and not $tookCase>>
    Hero: Watson, your hat. Mr Vance, we shall go at once. #line:100-015
    Toby: Thank you, sir. I'll run on ahead and open up the shop. #line:100-016
    <<walk toby 285 148>>
    <<hide toby>>
    <<set $tookCase to true>>
===

title: toby.look
---
A thin young man in a work coat two sizes too large, turning his cap round and round. #line:100-017
===

title: watson.look
---
<<loop watson 1>>
<<animate watson once>>
<<loop watson 0>>
<<cel watson 0>>
I am in my armchair, with yesterday's [i]Standard[/i], read twice over. #line:100-018
===

title: watson.talk
---
<<if $tookCase>>
Watson: I have my revolver, Holmes, if it comes to that. #line:100-019
<<else>>
Watson: The boy is frightened half out of his wits. Hear him out, Holmes. #line:100-020
<<endif>>
===

title: mantelLens.look
---
Holmes's lens, on the mantel where he left it. #line:100-021
===

title: mantelLens.do
---
<<hide mantelLens>>
<<get lens>>
<<set $hasLens to true>>
Hero: Where I go, it goes. #line:100-022
===

title: correspondence.look
---
Unanswered letters, pinned to the mantel with a jack-knife. #line:100-023
===

title: correspondence.do
---
Hero: They have waited a month. They can wait another night. #line:100-024
===

title: violin.look
---
Holmes's violin, laid across a chair. It has seen him through worse evenings. #line:100-025
===

title: bench.look
---
A rack of test tubes on the chemistry bench, and a stain Mrs Hudson has given up on. #line:100-026
===

title: slipper.look
---
The Persian slipper, where Holmes keeps his tobacco. #line:100-027
===

title: fire.look
---
A good fire. The only warm thing in London tonight. #line:100-028
===

title: window.look
---
Fog, thick as wool. The lamps across the street are smudges of yellow. #line:100-029
===

title: door.look
---
The door to the landing, and the seventeen steps down to the street. #line:100-030
===

title: door.do
---
<<if $tookCase and $hasLens>>
<<walk hero 285 148>>
<<animate door once>>
Watson: A cab, Holmes? #line:100-031
Hero: A cab, Watson. Clerkenwell. #line:100-032
<<room 101>>
<<elseif $tookCase>>
Hero: My lens, Watson. I shall want it tonight. #line:100-033
<<else>>
Hero: We have a visitor. It would be rude to leave before he has told us why he came. #line:100-034
<<endif>>
===
